{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/396551-tabletop-simulator","id":396551,"title":"Tabletop Simulator","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T11:37:26-08:00","id":396551,"title":"Tabletop Simulator","content":"Over at Steam there is a product coming out called Tabletop Simulator. It is meant to be an interactive sandbox for designing and playing table top games, from 1313 Dead End Drive to whatever lies the other side of Yahtzee. It is still in the developmental stage with user reviews being overwhelmingly positive. The <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/274930865/tabletop-simulator\" target=\"_blank\">Kickstarter</a> for it initiated a 1200% response, and has prompted the developers to provide early access and community cooperated development. Through the Steam Workshop, someone already initiated efforts for a NWoD pack.<br /> <br /> All of the above is an FYI. And this may be the way to go, but I would rather support Onyx Path more directly. I would attempt it myself, however, I cannot program. I have tried and failed to make computers do what I want for over 35 years. (Yes, when I started TRS-80s were on the drawing board and my first computer had a whopping 2k ram with a cassette tape backup.) Ideally, if I were to see something specific to the World of Darkness here I would want the program to:<br /> <br /> 1) directly access a file storing PDF documents (purchased through Drivethru and other legitimate sellers) with full search functionality,<br /> 2) direct access to each table in each PDF through a selection menu - one clicks on the game and book and a menu of the tables appears,<br /> 3) a similar menu tree for Story Teller screen tables,<br /> 4) a Story Teller modifiable template system for the different types of information sheets needed for play,<br /> 4a) various available official fonts and artwork for use with these sheets,<br /> 4b) these should also directly be able to incorporate those put together by Mr. Gone,<br /> 4c) ability to import ST and Player developed artwork as well as additional fonts,<br /> 5) in game browser that interacts with world map systems, map images, and building layouts,<br /> 5a) display of maps for scale with move-able miniatures<br /> 6) logins for ST, Asst. STs, and Players with appropriate permissions.<br /> 6a) ST has full access for editing all content,<br /> 6b) ASTs have access for content generation and game journal generation,<br /> 6c) Players have access to maintain character sheets and a character journal,<br /> 7) interactive capacity with VOIP systems such as Teamspeak 3 with Overwolf,<br /> 7a) icon set for TS and or other services of 16x16 vector art PNGs making identification of game, game roll (ST, AST, Player), character template (changeling, demon, mage, promethean, vampire, werewolf, wraith, etc.) and subdivision (cabal, clan, krewe, tribe, etc.) included,<br /> 8) graphical display for die rolling,<br /> 8a) ST die rolling conventions for silent secret roll (reveal-able if desired) and secret roll with ominous sound effect (reveal-able if desired),<br /> 8b) AST coordinated rolls observed by the ST and reveal-able by ST if desired - both silent and with sound effect,<br /> 8c) Player rolls (hidden and open) observed and released by the ST - once rolled they lock until the ST releases the roll,<br /> 8d) rolling conventions set by ST to be CWoD, NWoD, or hybrid.<br /> <br /> Program to be available to customers for $15? Service packs incorporating various art designs by game available at $10 each?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat does everyone think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,